fpu: the 68K softfloat from Previous and WinUAE

The 68881 computes in an 80-bit extended format: a 64-bit significand with
an explicit integer bit and a 15-bit exponent, rounded at every operation
to the precision and in the mode FPCR asks for. No host Basilisk II runs
on has that format in hardware outside x87, and none of the cores in fpu/
reproduces it everywhere:

  * fpu_ieee holds the register in a long double, which is x87's 80 bits
    on x86, a double under MSVC and on Apple silicon (53 bits, exponent to
    1e308), and IEEE binary128 on AArch64 Linux (more bits than the 68881,
    so its results are not the 68881's);
  * fpu_mpfr is exact and is what configure and the Xcode project choose on
    ARM and on macOS, at the price of GMP and MPFR as dependencies and a
    malloc and a free per floating-point instruction;
  * fpu_uae holds a double.

This adds, unused for now, the software model the Amiga and Atari
emulators settled on: SoftFloat 2a as maintained by QEMU, extended for the
68881/68882 by Andreas Grabher for the Previous NeXT emulator, with his
port of Motorola's 68040 FPSP for the transcendental functions — the
algorithms a 68040 Macintosh runs from its ROM for FSIN and the rest — and
packed decimal. It needs only 64-bit integer arithmetic, so it gives the
same bits on every host. The files are WinUAE's copy, as Hatari vendors it;
fpu/softfloat/README says where they come from, under which licences
(SoftFloat-2a, BSD, GPL-2.0-or-later), and the five changes made here:
include paths, WinUAE's logging headers, two undefined behaviours
(negating INT32_MIN or INT64_MIN, a 128-bit shift by 64), and
mul64To128() as one 128-bit multiply where the compiler has one (mul and
umulh on AArch64) instead of four 32-bit products. The arithmetic is
unchanged.

The next patch builds a core on it.

diff --git a/BasiliskII/src/uae_cpu_2021/fpu/softfloat/README b/BasiliskII/src/uae_cpu_2021/fpu/softfloat/README
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..8d6c0404
--- /dev/null
+++ b/BasiliskII/src/uae_cpu_2021/fpu/softfloat/README
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+68K softfloat
+=============
+
+An exact software model of the MC68881/MC68882 floating-point unit's
+arithmetic in its own 80-bit extended format, for fpu_softfloat.cpp. It
+needs only 64-bit integers, so it gives the same bits on every host: x86,
+AArch64 (Apple silicon, Linux, bare metal) and the rest. It needs no
+`long double`, no host floating-point state, and no library.
+
+Origin
+------
+
+- softfloat.c, softfloat.h, softfloat-macros.h, softfloat-specialize.h:
+  John R. Hauser's SoftFloat release 2a as maintained by QEMU, extended for
+  the 68881/68882 (SOFTFLOAT_68K: move, abs, neg, getexp, getman, scale,
+  rem, mod, sglmul, sgldiv, cmp, tst, 8- and 16-bit conversions,
+  denormal and unnormal operands, the internal values the exceptional-
+  operand frames need) by Andreas Grabher for the Previous NeXT emulator.
+- softfloat_fpsp.c, softfloat_fpsp_tables.h: the transcendental functions
+  (fsin, fcos, ftan, fsincos, fatan, fasin, facos, fetox, fetoxm1, ftwotox,
+  ftentox, flogn, flognp1, flog10, flog2, fsinh, fcosh, ftanh, fatanh),
+  Andreas Grabher's port to softfloat of Motorola's 68040 Floating Point
+  Software Package, the code a 68040 Macintosh runs for them from its ROM.
+- softfloat_decimal.c: packed decimal (the P format) to and from extended.
+
+The same code is WinUAE's and Hatari's softfloat FPU, and QEMU's m68k
+target carries the same FPSP port. These files are WinUAE's copy as
+vendored by Hatari at e77819f7, taken from the oracle tree of pom68k
+(github.com/habib256/pom68k, 6c4db1a, oracle/uae/upstream/softfloat/),
+which keeps that copy unchanged.
+
+Licence
+-------
+
+As stated in each file: the SoftFloat-2a licence, the BSD licence and
+GPL-2.0-or-later, all compatible with Basilisk II's GPL-2.0-or-later. The
+SoftFloat-2a terms ask that a derivative work say it is one and may
+contain errors: this file and the "macemu:" comments are that notice.
+
+Changes made here (each marked "macemu:" in the source)
+-------------------------------------------------------
+
+1. Include paths flattened: "softfloat/softfloat.h" and
+   "softfloat/softfloat-specialize.h" become "softfloat.h" and
+   "softfloat-specialize.h".
+2. softfloat_decimal.c no longer includes WinUAE's sysconfig.h and
+   sysdeps.h, which served only its logging, off unless DECIMAL_LOG is set.
+3. int32_to_floatx80() and int64_to_floatx80() form the magnitude in
+   unsigned arithmetic: negating INT32_MIN or INT64_MIN was a signed
+   overflow.
+4. shortShift128Left() accepts a count of 64, which normalising a
+   significand whose high half is zero asks for; a C shift by 64 is
+   undefined. Both were found by pom68k under ASan/UBSan.
+5. mul64To128() multiplies in one unsigned __int128 where the compiler has
+   it - mul and umulh on AArch64 - instead of four 32-bit products. The
+   product is the same; every operation that multiplies significands is
+   cheaper.
+
+The arithmetic itself is unchanged.
